# ChoreTracker — Cursor Rules
# Global rules. Applied to every prompt in this project without exception.

---

## Project Context

ChoreTracker is a mobile-first PWA for families. Two distinct user surfaces: Parent and Child.
Never mix concerns between the parent and child surfaces.

Always read these files before making any structural decision:
- Architecture.md
- TechnicalDecisions.md
- DesignPrinciples.md
- BuildPlan.md

---

## Stack (Locked)

- Framework: Next.js App Router + TypeScript
- Styling: Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui
- Database: Neon (Postgres) via Prisma
- SMS: Twilio
- Deployment: Vercel

Do not introduce new dependencies without explicitly flagging it and waiting for approval.

---

## TypeScript

- Never use `any`. Use `unknown` and narrow, or define the type.
- Use generics when a function needs to be reusable and type-safe.
- Prefer discriminated unions for state machines (chore status, proposal status).

---

## Component Architecture

- No inline functions in JSX. Extract named handlers above the return statement.
- No inline layout (grid, flex) in page files. Use named layout components.
- If a div has more than 4 Tailwind classes and appears more than once, extract it into a named component.
- All conditional class merging via `cn()` from shadcn. Never template-string classes together.
- Use `cva()` for component variants. Never branch on className strings inline.
- Components live in external files. Never define a component inside another component file.
- Files should be under 120 lines wherever possible. If a file is growing beyond that, extract.

---

## File Structure

- `src/components/ui/` — shadcn primitives. Do not edit directly.
- `src/components/layout/` — page-level layout wrappers.
- `src/components/parent/` — all parent surface components.
- `src/components/child/` — all child surface components.
- `src/components/shared/` — components used by both surfaces.
- `src/lib/` — utilities, prisma client, twilio client, cn helper.
- `src/app/` — Next.js App Router pages and API routes only. No business logic here.

---

## React Conventions

- Default to Server Components. Add `'use client'` only when required (interactivity, hooks, browser APIs).
- No data fetching inside `useEffect`. Use Server Components or React Query.
- Twilio API calls are server-side only. Never expose Twilio credentials to the client.
- Set `export const maxDuration = 60` on all API routes that call Twilio.

---

## Behavior Rules

- Plan before code. State which files will be touched and what will change. Wait for approval.
- Do not refactor unrelated code in the same session.
- Do not modify the Prisma schema without flagging it explicitly.
- Surface architectural tradeoffs before implementing — do not bury them in code.
- Errors never reach the user as raw exceptions. Surface as non-blocking UI feedback.

---

## Design Rules

- Mobile-first. Every layout, tap target, and interaction is designed for a phone screen first.
- Minimal friction. Core actions reachable in as few taps as possible.
- No confirmation dialogs except for destructive or financial actions (Pay modal, delete).

